# Project Instructions — claude_researcher

Full runtime instructions live upstream in `template/RESEARCHER.md`. At session start, clone the upstream template and read `RESEARCHER.md` from the clone.

## Credentials

```bash
TOKEN="<TOKEN>"
USERNAME="<USERNAME>"
REPO="<REPO>"
```

`<TOKEN>` is your fine-grained GitHub PAT, scoped to read `<USERNAME>/basic_config` and read/write `<USERNAME>/<REPO>`. `<REPO>` is just the repo name (not `owner/repo`). Do not commit these values anywhere.

## Session start

Your **first action** is to clone the upstream template, then read `RESEARCHER.md` from the clone:

```bash
git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/danparshall/claude_researcher.git /home/claude/.claude_researcher_template
```

Then read `/home/claude/.claude_researcher_template/template/RESEARCHER.md` and follow its session-start sequence.

**Fallback if the clone fails:**

```
WebFetch https://raw.githubusercontent.com/danparshall/claude_researcher/main/template/RESEARCHER.md
```

The raw-CDN path can be stale by 24+ hours after upstream changes; surface the clone failure to the user before relying on the fallback.

### Ordering

Before any other tool calls — including `conversation_search`, `recent_chats`, or reading any files other than `RESEARCHER.md` itself — perform the clone (or fallback fetch) and read `RESEARCHER.md`. Past-chat search tools are available but should not be called at session start; the canonical history of the user's work is in their research repo's `STATUS.md` and `RESEARCH_LOG.md`, which `RESEARCHER.md` will direct you to. If the user references past work, `RESEARCHER.md` tells you how to look it up.

If anything in this file looks inconsistent with the user's actual setup (wrong username, wrong repo, expired token), stop and surface the mismatch before doing any work.
